<title>USA: Bio-Technology says court won't hear case.</title>
<headline>Bio-Technology says court won't hear case.</headline>
<dateline>ISELIN, N.J. 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bio-Technology General Corp said Tuesday that the U.S. Supreme Court declined to hear its case concerning its human growth hormone, Bio-Tropin, and it has no expectation of selling it in the country &quot;in the coming few years.&quot;  </p>
<p>A preliminary injunction barring the company from selling the product in the United States was issued in August 1995. The injunction was issued after Genentech Inc filed a patent-infringement claim.</p>
<p>The company also said Tuesday that Bio-Tropin has received marketing approval from the Brazilian Minister of Health.</p>
<p>The product is expected to be launched in the next couple of months.</p>
<p>Bio-Tropin is now marketed in 19 countries around the world, the company said.</p>
</text>
